<title>MAURITANIA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>MAURITANIA GOVERNMENT LIST (961013)</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> * 13 Oct 96 - Results from the October 11 elections showed  *</p>
<p> *		 the ruling Democratic and Social Republican   *</p>
<p> *		 Party had won 60 of the 79 seats in the new   *</p>
<p> *		 national assembly. Most of the rest of the    *</p>
<p> *		 seats will be decided in run-off votes on     *</p>
<p> *		 October 18.					     *</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p>			     - - - - - -</p>
<p> President.....................Col Maaouya Ould Sid'Ahmed TAYA</p>
<p>				    (sworn in 18 Apr 92 for 6-yr term)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>CABINET (Formed 20 April 1992, reshuffled 6 May 96):</p>
<p>Prime Minister (Apptd 2 Jan</p>
<p>     96)....................Cheikh El Afia Ould Mohamed KHOUNA</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Civil Service, Labour,</p>
<p>     Youth &amp; Sports.............Sidi Mohamed Ould Mohamed VALL</p>
<p> Communication (information),</p>
<p>     Parliamentary Relations.................Rachid Ould SALEH</p>
<p> Culture, Islamic Affairs................Mohamed Ould MBOIRICK</p>
<p> Defence...................................Abdallahi Ould ABDI</p>
<p> Education......................................Baba Ould SIDI</p>
<p> Finance...................................Camara Ali GUELADIO</p>
<p> Fisheries, Maritime Economy................Abdallahi Ould NEM</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs &amp;</p>
<p>     Cooperation......Lemrabott Sidi Mahmoud Ould Cheikh AHMED</p>
<p> Health, Social Affairs.........................SOW Abou Demba</p>
<p> Interior, Post &amp;</p>
<p>     Telecommunications...................Dah Ould Abdel JELIL</p>
<p> Justice.......................Ethmane Ould Sid'Ahmed EL YESSA</p>
<p> Mining &amp; Industry........................N'gaide Lamine KAYOU</p>
<p> Planning....................................Mohamed Ould AMAR</p>
<p> Rural Development &amp;</p>
<p> Environment.......Mohamed Lemine Ch'bih Ould Cheick MALAININE</p>
<p> Secretary-General of the Presidency.Colonel Ahmed Ould MINNIH</p>
<p> Trade, Craft, Tourism.....................Bodiel Ould HOUMEID</p>
<p> Transport, Supplies.........................SOW Mohamed Deina</p>
<p> Water, Energy.......................Mohamed Lemine Ould AHMED</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor.........................Ahmed Ould ZEIN</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
